    {
      "id": 149996,
      "name": "Foote",
      "username": "Foote",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-10-30T13:53:37.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Praion\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/p/e9bcb4/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Praion:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>From the description it seems like Fixer has come down from his post regeneration Rage and is more rounded now. What does he do now though? Does he still use normal tools as weapons or has the way he fights changed now? Asking for Roleplaying reasons…</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Like most characters in Tactics, there is a strong sense of change and growth as the story progresses. Mr. Fixer will be no different in that regard. I can't go into specifics because I'd like to keep being a playtester, but you will notice a bit of an evolution in his fighting style and philosophy.&nbsp;</p>",
